  "scope": "Local Darwin arm64 isolated actual canonical server and sealed CLI. HTTP is the protected loopback exchange; EdDSA/ES256 evidence additionally exercises actual native admission with a new Device/signing key. No Linux/remote/provider/model-host/package or Gate6 acceptance qualification.",
  "implementation": [
    "POST /v2/credentials admits a current ordinary administrator before bounded JSON parsing, refuses hostile Host/Origin/provider/Upgrade headers and missing owned HTTP/1.1 custody, and shares one five-second admission/handler deadline.",
    "Response custody is generalized behind a private Send owner interface. The issuance wrapper retains Store authority fences and shared capacity until actual socket IO ends; Body EOS does not release either. Current expiry, disconnect and runtime cancellation fence delivery. Success and typed rejection disable caching and close the connection.",
    "ApplicationClient exposes explicit typed issuance and cancellation with complete normalized intent correlation, profile/current issued-time/expiry/secret/server-ID checks, sanitized failures and no retry or authority fallback. Task mode refuses this API.",
    "Protected OpenAPI describes the wire request/outcome/error statuses, literal set normalization, independent issuance semantics and physical custody. Endpoint inventory now covers24 declarations and25 explicit HTTP methods. Full /v1/operations body parity remains separate."
  ],
