  "cases": [
    "Two new actual production functions pass. For both signing algorithms, send an original issuance request then disconnect before observing a response; explicit SDK replay recovers a single stable result, normalized replay is equal and changed expiry conflicts. This first disconnect leaves acceptance uncertain; it does not assert that the first transaction had already committed.",
    "Public provisioning enrolls a fresh Device and signing key against the returned child ID; exact enrollment replays agree. Actual CanonicalClient opens and shuts down before and after same-address server restart. Original issuance then returns the identical ID/secret/issued time/expiry. Public child revocation refuses saved issuance and native admission.",
    "Actual raw HTTP proves authentication precedes malformed JSON, ordinary nonadmin/model-shaped credentials refuse, Host/Origin/provider/Upgrade and caller-supplied assurance refuse, malformed/oversized bodies have structured bounded errors, and intended success closes the socket without caching. Current original issuer revocation refuses saved recovery.",
    "Four client unit functions pass:18 issuance outcome cases cover every immutable request field, server IDs, secret, profile, issued time/expiry, unknown fields, status and sanitized error; cancellation/invalid/admin intent and Task mode do not send. Existing human-consent SDK checks pass.",
    "Six existing actual record socket functions pass after custody generalization: HTTP backpressure, expiry, disconnect, shutdown; HTTPS backpressure and expiry/shutdown. They retain credentials/records through physical writes and release guards/capacity on terminal IO. Their large record metadata fixtures prove the shared writer mechanism; small issuance metadata was not artificially padded to force backpressure.",
    "Fresh actual sealed CLI init/serve check passes74 wire exchanges with73 schema checks, including22 issuance/revocation cases and the preceding Task/artifact matrix. Task creation remains setup-only. SIGTERM exits0 and HTTP/MCP listeners close; parent and issued child secrets are absent from server logs. Raw secret-bearing samples remain private.",
    "All1298 guarded crate/example/contract/embedded inputs remain unchanged through build and runtime. No strip/LLVM failure. Initial build01 fails on a client module/re-export collision; implementation module renamed and clean build02 completes in637.1s, dominated by shared service/MCP rebuild."
  ],
  "development_record": [
    {
      "status": "retained failed compile",
      "path": ".local/gate-6/scoped-issuance-http/build-01.jsonl",
      "sha256": "2a3338399afda6c89f259d23086d89e15d79332df605143726dcb27d789ffd42",
      "detail": "E0255 client implementation module and public protocol namespace had the same name. Fixed by naming the implementation module issuance; no public compatibility alias added."
    }
  ],
  "remaining": [
    "Replace old generic CLI issue with protected saved-intent native installation/resume and fresh Device/key assets, including partial-file/failure recovery and actual CLI proof.",
    "Further issuance-specific expiry/tombstone/cancellation failure cases remain distinct from the shared physical record IO regression evidence.",
    "Complete full named /v1/operations body parity, remaining MCP consultation/movement and actual supported host/profile work; retain unresolved intermittent provider-uncertainty regression.",
    "G6-065 remains in progress and all105 Gate6 tasks remain active; publication separate."
  ],
